        narrative: "Koh Larn is the reason to be here. It is a forty-minute ferry or a fifteen-minute speedboat offshore and the water is a completely different proposition from Pattaya's own beach — clear, swimmable, with several separate bays so you can get away from the busiest one. Samae and Nual are quieter than Tawaen, which is where the day-trip boats land.\n\nHere is the honest constraint: a full-day island trip runs about six hours and does not fit around an evening flight. Pattaya to Suvarnabhumi is 1.5 to 2 hours and you want an hour of buffer on top of that. If your flight is after 8pm you can do the island and go straight to the airport with bags in the car. If it is earlier, do a short morning — a sunset-and-viewpoint run the evening before instead, and a slow beach breakfast on the last day.\n\nThe one thing not to do is book a full-day boat and a 4pm flight and hope. Boats come back late, the motorway does not care about your booking, and this is the single most common way a four-day Thailand trip ends badly.",
        tours: ["/thailand/pattaya/koh-larn-coral-island-full-day-tour", "/thailand/pattaya/pattaya-marina-night-market-sunset-tour"],
